  <data name="label35.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>GENERAL: 
Simulate Orbits/Hyperbolas - Enables/disables visualization of all or just hyperbolic orbits.
Small-Scale Timewarp - Changes to a timewarp ranging from 1x to 5 000x.
Precision Factor - Sets the minimum precision factor, higher number means less precise.
Orbit Draw Limit - Higher the number the more orbits will be drawn.
Reset - Resets the whole simulation.
PRESETS:
List of pre-made systems ready to be loaded.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="label36.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>By focusing on a spaceship you are able to control it.
- A/D - Rotate the ship when FREE is selected.
- Shift - Increases thrust. Shown on the bar on the right side of the screen.
              *thrust only works in small-scale timewarp*

HEADING CONTROLS
- The ship automatically points to the chosen heading.  </value>
  </data>
  <data name="label38.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>There are four types or bodies:
- Black Holes - Apears with a mass above 6e32 kg.
- Stars - Apears with a mass above 2e29 kg.
            - Their color depends on mass.
- Planets - They apear with a mass above 1e7 kg.
- Spaceships - Anything with a mass below 1e7 kg.
             - Can be controled by focusing on it.</value>
  </data>
